course: dictionary
lesson: 4298
title: Words from legends
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Griffin is a noun, and it names an imaginary creature from myths and legends. It has the head, wings and claws of an eagle and the body of a lion. «A Gryphon, or griffin, is a creature of old legends with the head and wings of an eagle and the body of a lion; it never existed.» The words «old legends» and «it never existed» are clues that it is not a real animal.
explain: The same creature can have more than one spelling. «A Gryphon (also spelled griffin) is a creature from old stories.» The brackets tell you that gryphon and griffin mean the same thing. Griffon is a third spelling you may see.
explain: Griffin is also a surname, which is a family name, so it can belong to a person. A capital G at the start of a name often means it is a person's name, not a creature. Read the words around it to decide which meaning is right.
explain: Writers use a griffin to show something strong, proud and watchful. The phrase «a griffin guarding gold» gives a picture of a powerful creature keeping treasure safe.
fact: A griffin is an imaginary creature from myths and legends.
fact: A griffin has the head, wings and claws of an eagle and the body of a lion.
fact: Gryphon and griffon are other spellings of the same creature.
fact: Griffin can also be a surname, a family name for people.
fact: Some historians think ancient people may have imagined griffins from old fossils, but this is an idea, not something proven.
exercise: «A Gryphon, or griffin, is a creature of old legends.» What is a griffin? | A kind of castle with high walls | *An imaginary creature with an eagle's head and wings and a lion's body | A real bird that lives in the desert
exercise: Which word is another spelling of griffin? | *gryphon | wyvern | phoenix
exercise: What is Griffin in «Mia Griffin lives next door»? | *A family name | A creature with wings | A kind of treasure | A type of castle
test: What is a griffin often shown guarding in stories? | *Gold | A school | A river | Snow
test: Why might a story use a griffin to show strength? | It is a funny joke | *It shows strength, pride and careful watching | It is a real animal from the zoo | It shows the creature is weak and sleepy
exam: Which clue in «A Gryphon, or griffin, is a creature of old legends» shows that a griffin is not real? | *old legends | the head and wings of an eagle | the body of a lion | a creature from old stories
